  "sourceAnimationModule": {
    "archiveFile": "_next/static/chunks/0j~ix342hy.sg.js",
    "bytes": 55432,
    "sha256": "f8f02fc84097ac74933c62abdbf3f3ef676621bdc450f0686ac106fea836ed69",
    "sourceOpening": "The invitation video cross-fades over its poster; poster removal follows the first video time update after 0.05s. The hero background starts when video time remaining is below 1.8s, its names fade in after 0.8s, and the cover begins a 2s ease-in-out fade when 1s remains. The cover is removed after that opacity transition completes.",
    "sourceReveals": "Section wrappers use initial opacity 0 and y 40px, once at 15% visibility with a -60px bottom viewport margin, 0.9s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1). Program rows use initial y 20px, once at 40% visibility, 0.6s ease-out with 0.05s stagger (the Chorlove motion runtime default).",
    "adaptation": "The source page module depends on the Chorlove React/Framer Motion runtime. These exact template-level timings and thresholds are adapted in the isolated bridge and CSS; captured page markup, CSS, assets, and SVG motion remain unchanged. Reduced motion opens immediately, reveals the hero, pauses video/SVG motion, and removes transitions."
  },
  "notes": [
    "The archive preview snapshot is preserved byte-for-byte. The isolated runnable page retains all 12 captured sections and removes captured Next.js/site scripts.",
    "All referenced images and video are packaged locally. Seven absent archive images were recovered from their exact Chorlove URLs.",
    "Captured Lace typography references Instrument Serif, Monsieur La Doulaise, and Ballet Clean. Google Fonts CSS and WOFF2 files are retained with source provenance and served locally.",
    "The six original gallery pictures are preserved as captured assets; runtime replaces them with shared-contract gallery entries or empty preview placeholders.",
    "The captured Bellagio cover overlay and video are retained; the isolated bridge follows source-module time-update and transition timing rather than a fixed timeout."
  ]
}
